WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
You offered advice. Why did your friend go quiet?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
Perhaps advice arrived before understanding.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
A 2014 study compared responses in initial interactions.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
Active listening was one response style examined.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
Limited settings cannot guarantee every relationship improves.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
Attend to the experience they describe.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
Offer a tentative reflection.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
“That felt disappointing?” leaves room for correction.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
Then check what kind of help is wanted.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
Understanding a feeling need not endorse every judgment.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
You do not have to carry every problem.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
Safety and appropriate support come first.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
Ask: listen for a while, or explore solutions?

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Respect a wish not to talk.

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
Listening needs practice and boundaries.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
Sometimes it helps to leave a little more space.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
Allow someone to finish their own story.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
Leave the next words to the person speaking.
